-- TESTING -------------------------------------------------------------------
  Tested      Bare steps and smooth .nex builds played by the owner on a
              Spectrum Next, 2026-11-23; this patch through the real loader
              not yet played

  Replay      1.0 (2026-11-23, nexclash add-hard-drivin, PR
              bleughb/nexclash#306; auto PASSED, stamped selftest --verify
              PASSED): the owner's recording, 22,116 frames, 1,555 updates.
              Steps build: each update run by the build's model (sub-steps at
              28 MHz, the Next's paging) and by an independent spec of the
              sub-step rules from the same state, adaptive N and fixed N = 1 /
              2 / 4: 6,220 cases, 0 mismatches (N = 1 also equals the
              recording); unit tests and 20 of 20 negative controls caught;
              model pace per update 10.00 / 10.19 / 10.76 frames (median / p95
              / max; 10 = real time). Original time steps: 3,112 checks of the
              real update and 3,281 in-between views, 0 fail. ROM paths: every
              byte the game runs is as recorded.

  Emulator    JNext: the steps prototype (the same sub-step code), 154 s: 120
              race-clock seconds in 120.12 s; the smooth route timed against
              the plain build, 178 updates. This patch's build not run in
              JNext.

  Coverage    The owner's recording of play from the title screen (22,116
              frames). Not covered: stopwatch against the race clock on
              hardware, race end and the replay menus, 9 replays and No
              crashes on recorded play (synthetic states only), joystick.

  Hardware    Bare .nex builds on a Spectrum Next, played by the owner: the
              steps build "plays much better"; the smooth build plays like the
              original. This patch (loading screen, trainers, through the real
              loader) not yet run on hardware.

  Nothing here claims a result on real hardware unless the line above says so.

-- HOW TO USE ----------------------------------------------------------------
  Put this .nxc and the game file in the same folder on the Next's card and
  choose the .nxc in the Browser. See README.txt.
